### HTTP Test Scripts for OrderItems V4 Endpoint - Null Value Testing
### Base URL - adjust if needed
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4004
@servicePath = /odata/v4/orders

### Step 0: Get first Order (execute this first!)
### This automatically captures the Order ID for all subsequent requests
# @name getFirstOrder
GET {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders?$top=1&$orderby=createdAt desc HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

### Order ID is automatically set from Step 0 response
@orderId = {{getFirstOrder.response.body.value[0].ID}}

### Step 1: (Optional) Create a new Order if needed
### Only use this if you want to create a specific test order
### After creating, you can either:
###   a) Re-run Step 0 to use the new order, or
###   b) Copy the ID from response and set @orderId manually
POST {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "OrderNo": "TEST-NULL-001",
  "buyer": "test@test.de",
  "IsActiveEntity": true
}

### Step 2: Create multiple OrderItems with various null value scenarios (combines previous Steps 2-7)
# NOTE: OrderItems is draft-enabled and must be created via Orders deep insert
# NOTE: quantity is mandatory (Common.FieldControl: #Mandatory) so it cannot be null
# This single request creates 6 OrderItems testing:
#   - PROD-001: All nullable fields set to null (tests explicit null assignment)
#   - PROD-002: Fields omitted (tests "no update" behavior - omitted fields should not be touched)
#   - PROD-003: Empty string "" vs null for string field (tests that "" is different from null)
#   - PROD-004: Zero vs null for numeric fields (tests that 0 is different from null)
#   - PROD-005: False vs null for boolean field (tests that false is different from null)
#   - PROD-006: Baseline with all fields populated (for PATCH operations in Steps 8-12)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Items": [
    {
      "product_ID": "PROD-001",
      "quantity": 1,
      "title": null,
      "price": null,
      "validFrom": null,
      "timestamp": null,
      "date": null,
      "time": null,
      "boolean": null,
      "decimal": null,
      "byte": null
    },
	{
      "product_ID": "PROD-002",
      "quantity": 10
    },
	{
      "product_ID": "PROD-003",
      "quantity": 5,
      "title": "",
      "price": 100.50
    },
	{
      "product_ID": "PROD-004",
      "quantity": 0,
      "price": 0.0,
      "decimal": 0.000,
      "byte": 0,
      "title": "Zero Values Test"
    },
	{
      "product_ID": "PROD-005",
      "quantity": 1,
      "boolean": false,
      "title": "Boolean False Test"
    },
	{
      "product_ID": "PROD-006",
      "quantity": 15,
      "title": "Baseline Test Product",
      "price": 99.99,
      "validFrom": "2025-01-15T10:30:00Z",
      "timestamp": "2025-01-15T10:30:00.123Z",
      "date": "2025-01-15",
      "time": "10:30:00",
      "boolean": true,
      "decimal": 123.456,
      "byte": 255
    }
  ]
}

### Step 2a: Get the latest OrderItem ID (execute after Step 2, before Steps 3-7)
### This fetches PROD-006 (baseline OrderItem) created in Step 2 for PATCH operations
# @name getLatestOrderItem
GET {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true)/Items?$top=1 HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

### OrderItem ID is automatically set from Step 2a response
@orderItemId = {{getLatestOrderItem.response.body.value[0].ID}}

### Step 3: PATCH OrderItem - Set string field to null
# Execute Step 2a first to automatically capture the OrderItem ID (PROD-006 from Step 2)
# OrderItems are draft-enabled, so we patch via Orders navigation
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true)/Items(ID='{{orderItemId}}',IsActiveEntity=false) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": null
}

### Step 4: PATCH OrderItem - Set numeric field to null
# NOTE: quantity cannot be null (mandatory field), so this will fail for quantity
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true)/Items(ID='{{orderItemId}}',IsActiveEntity=false) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": null,
  "decimal": null
}

### Step 5: PATCH OrderItem - Omit fields (should not change them)
# This should not modify any fields
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true)/Items(ID='{{orderItemId}}',IsActiveEntity=false) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_ID": "PROD-UPDATED"
}

### Step 6: PATCH OrderItem - Set boolean to null
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true)/Items(ID='{{orderItemId}}',IsActiveEntity=false) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "boolean": null
}

### Step 7: PATCH OrderItem - Set date/time fields to null
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true)/Items(ID='{{orderItemId}}',IsActiveEntity=false) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "validFrom": null,
  "timestamp": null,
  "date": null,
  "time": null
}

### Step 8: Invalid test - Empty string for numeric field (should fail with 400/422)
# This should fail because "" is not a valid number
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Items": [
    {
      "product_ID": "PROD-007",
      "quantity": "",
      "title": "Invalid Empty String for Number"
    }
  ]
}

### Step 9: Invalid test - String "NULL" for numeric field (should fail with 400/422)
# This should fail because "NULL" string is not a valid number
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Items": [
    {
      "product_ID": "PROD-008",
      "quantity": "NULL",
      "title": "Invalid NULL String for Number"
    }
  ]
}

### Step 10: Invalid test - Empty string for boolean field (should fail with 400/422)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Items": [
    {
      "product_ID": "PROD-009",
      "quantity": 1,
      "boolean": "",
      "title": "Invalid Empty String for Boolean"
    }
  ]
}

### Step 11: Invalid test - Empty string for date field (should fail with 400/422)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/Orders(ID='{{orderId}}',IsActiveEntity=true) HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Items": [
    {
      "product_ID": "PROD-010",
      "quantity": 1,
      "date": "",
      "title": "Invalid Empty String for Date"
    }
  ]
}

### Step 12: Query created OrderItems to verify null values
GET {{baseUrl}}{{servicePath}}/OrderItems?$filter=order_ID eq '{{orderId}}'&$orderby=product_ID HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

